# Pad script for the harness probe: "FRAME BUTTONS", held from that program
# frame until the next line. '+' combines buttons, NONE releases all.
#
#   probe.exe ... --pad-script harness/scripts/pacman_demo.pad
#
# Drives pacman_2d and pacman_3d -- they run the same simulation -- through a
# route that eats a power pellet early and then tours the top half of the
# maze. It ends around frame 400 having scored about 1400 without dying.
#
# Two things to know before editing it.
#
# The numbers are four frames per tile: Pac-Man moves 2 pixels a frame and a
# tile is 8. And he is ALREADY MOVING at frame 0 -- the pad only sets which
# way he WANTS to go next, so he keeps running in his current direction until
# a turn becomes legal. A direction issued mid-corridor therefore takes effect
# at the next junction that allows it, not where it was issued, which is why
# "UP" at frame 86 rather than 94 is the difference between turning up at
# column 6 and turning up at column 9.
#
# Nothing here reacts to the ghosts. Run it much past frame 400 and Pac-Man
# will eventually be caught standing still in a corner; that is the script
# running out, not the game misbehaving.

0    LEFT      # already running left off the spawn tile, eating along row 20
46   DOWN      # down the left edge to the power pellet at the bottom corner
60   UP        # back up to the long bottom corridor
72   RIGHT
86   UP        # turns up at column 6 and climbs to the top corridor
152  RIGHT     # all the way across row 5
234  DOWN      # down the right edge
248  LEFT
270  UP        # up column 21 to the top row
300  LEFT
330  DOWN
350  LEFT      # back west along row 5
